What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/gc_idle
Date:		July 2013
Contact:	"Namjae Jeon" <namjae.jeon@samsung.com>
Description:
		 Select the requested GC mode: 0 normal, 1 idle cost-benefit,
		 2 idle greedy, 3 idle age-threshold (requires atgc mount option).
		 Reads return the requested GC_* mode name, shared with gc_urgent.
		 The last write to either node wins; 0 restores normal. Rapid GC
		 temporarily uses HIGH without changing the requested mode.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/atgc_candidate_ratio
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	F2FS maintainers
Description:
		 Read/write candidate percentage, range 0..100, default 20.
		 The four writable ATGC names follow android13-5.15 commit
		 3f0fd7f6624d7b99bd8d93cbcfe0241bc92d6448. Parameter writes
		 are serialized with victim selection and apply to subsequent
		 selections; they neither enable ATGC nor change the mount option.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/atgc_candidate_count
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	F2FS maintainers
Description:
		 Read/write candidate count, range 0..4294967295, default 10
		 sections. As in the reference implementation, the search budget
		 is max(count, ratio * victim_count / 100), not a hard cap of 10.
		 Zero is accepted; traversal remains bounded by available victims.
		 Percentage multiplication uses 64-bit arithmetic to avoid overflow.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/atgc_age_weight
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	F2FS maintainers
Description:
		 Read/write age weight, range 0..100, default 60 percent.
		 Valid-block weight is 100 minus this value.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/atgc_age_threshold
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	F2FS maintainers
Description:
		 Read/write unsigned 64-bit age threshold in seconds, range
		 0..18446744073709551615, default 259200 (three days), deliberately
		 retained locally instead of the reference's 604800 (seven days).
		 Values outside the range are rejected, never truncated to 32 bits.
		 Candidates younger than this threshold are skipped; the existing
		 no-victim retry with threshold zero when elapsed mounted time is
		 below the threshold is unchanged. This is not the activation gate.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/atgc_enabled
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	F2FS maintainers
Description:
		 Local read-only extension, 0 or 1. Reports actual ATGC activation,
		 not merely the presence of the atgc mount option. Activation is
		 decided at mount initialization: atgc must be requested and stored
		 accumulated mounted time must be at least 259200 seconds. There
		 is no live timer activation; remount cannot toggle atgc. Runtime
		 tuning, including age_threshold, does not change this state.
		 All F2FS sysfs paths now use /sys/fs/f2fs, and procfs uses
		 /proc/fs/f2fs, replacing f2fs_dev without compatibility aliases.

