What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/current_reserved_blocks
Date:		October 2017
Contact:	"Yunlong Song" <yunlong.song@huawei.com>
Contact:	"Chao Yu" <yuchao0@huawei.com>
Description:
		 Shows current reserved blocks in system, it may be temporarily
		 smaller than target_reserved_blocks, but will gradually
		 increase to target_reserved_blocks when more free blocks are
		 freed by user later.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/gc_urgent
Date:		August 2017
Contact:	"Jaegeuk Kim" <jaegeuk@kernel.org>
Description:
		 Write 0 for normal, 1 urgent HIGH, 2 urgent LOW, 3 urgent MID.
		 Other values are rejected. Reads return the requested GC_* mode
		 name (also for modes selected through gc_idle), not the temporary
		 rapid-GC override. LOW bypasses idle time for GC/discard only;
		 MID bypasses idle time and runs periodically without HIGH's
		 greedy victim selection or forced SSR. Outstanding I/O is still
		 checked by is_idle for LOW/MID. HIGH bypasses the GC idle gate.
		 Rapid GC temporarily selects HIGH, then restores the user mode.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/gc_urgent_sleep_time
Date:		August 2017
Contact:	"Jaegeuk Kim" <jaegeuk@kernel.org>
Description:
		 Controls HIGH/MID GC sleep time in milliseconds (default 500).
		 Values must be in 1..UINT_MAX. Rapid GC keeps its 1 ms interval.
		 Requires a running GC thread; absent thread returns EINVAL.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/gc_urgent_high_remaining
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-f2fs-devel@lists.sourceforge.net
Description:
		 Set the remaining user HIGH trial count; 0 disables the limit
		 (default). Each user HIGH background round consumes one trial.
		 Rapid GC, merged foreground work and other modes consume none.
		 Once exhausted, the next HIGH round restores normal. Writes are
		 serialized with mode changes; a positive budget is at most UINT_MAX.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/gc_segment_mode
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-f2fs-devel@lists.sourceforge.net
Description:
		 Select the gc_reclaimed_segments counter: 0 normal, 1 idle CB,
		 2 idle greedy, 3 idle AT, 4 urgent HIGH, 5 urgent LOW, 6 urgent MID.
		 Reads return the corresponding GC_* mode name; default is normal.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/gc_reclaimed_segments
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-f2fs-devel@lists.sourceforge.net
Description:
		 Per-effective-mode unsigned segment-processing counter, matching
		 GC segment statistics (not necessarily a fully freed section).
		 Rapid GC is charged to HIGH. Write 0 to reset the selected counter;
		 other writes are rejected. Counters are best-effort statistics and
		 may race reset/read with GC or wrap at UINT_MAX.

What:		/sys/fs/f2fs/<disk>/readdir_ra
Date:		November 2017
